# Declare binary content explicitly. Without this, git falls back to guessing
# from NUL bytes in the first 8k — which the shipped .wav assets happen to pass
# and a small all-ASCII PDF does NOT. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) a misclassified file gets its LFs rewritten to CRLF on checkout,
# which shifts every byte offset in a PDF xref table and silently corrupts it.
# Guessing right today is not a guarantee; declare it.
*.pdf     binary
*.wav     binary
*.png     binary
*.ico     binary
*.sqlite  binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.zip     binary
